thout World Cup support [Estimate]\n2. FY27 guidance with quantified margin targets (Nov 2026 Investor Day expected) [Unconfirmed]\n3. KOF Brazil volume momentum (record Q2 2026 volumes) [Estimate, web]\n4. Continued dividend increases + extraordinary distributions [Estimate]\n5. Potential disposal of Valora if integration fails [Assumption]\n\n**Risks (next 12 months):**\n1. Mexico excise-tax expansion (2026 non-alcoholic beverage excise already hurt KOF Mexico) [Estimate]\n2. Fed hike (market ~1/3 probability) \u2192 peso correction \u2192 ADR de-rating [Estimate]\n3. Tiendas 3B acceleration [Estimate]\n4. Levi & Korsinsky securities investigation \u2014 unresolved [Unconfirmed]\n5. Minimum-wage/labor reform in Mexico [Assumption]\n6. 2027 Mexican budget (Sept\u2013Nov 2026) containing new taxes\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 7.5. CORRELATION-ADJUSTED RISK (v2.0)\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n- **Common bear trigger across the portfolio:** a US reflation shock (Fed hike) would simultaneously (a) raise the USD discount rate, (b) pressure the peso, and (c) compress EM equity multiples. FMX is a high-bear-correlation asset *in that specific scenario*.\n- Tail correlation: FMX's ADR has historically been correlated with MXN carry trades; during 2022 stress, FEMSA fell 20%+. Conditional VaR (worst 5% quarter): \u221225\u201330% [Estimate]\n- Mitigation: the 5% dividend yield and defensive OXXO cash flows provide a partial floor; avoid if the portfolio is already short-MXN or long-EM.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 8. MONITORING RULES\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n**Thesis integrity thresholds:**\n1. OXXO Mexico quarterly SSS (ex-World Cup): \u22654% in Q3-26 and Q4-26 \u2192 thesis alive; <2% \u2192 re-evaluate\n2. OXXO traffic: any quarter with traffic <0% \u2192 downgrade thesis\n3. Consolidated operating margin: FY26 \u22658.0% and FY27 \u22658.5% \u2192 on-track; if FY27 <8.0%, base case fails\n4. KOF Mexico volume: quarterly decline >3% YoY \u2192 red flag (excise/share loss)\n5. USD/MXN: if >19.5, expect ADR underperformance; if <16.5, the peso strength is a continued headwind for USD investors\n6. Capital allocation: any new large M&A (>$1B) \u2192 reassess the whole thesis (Valora scar)\n7. Share count: SBC-driven dilution >0.5%/yr \u2192 deduct from FCF\n8. Dividend: ordinary dividend coverage <1.5x FCF \u2192 risk signal\n\n**Step 7-4. Pre-mortem \u2014 three failure scenarios with early warnings:**\n- (a) *The 3B war*: OXXO loses the value shopper; early warning = OXXO SSS <2% while 3B SSS >15% for 3 straight quarters.\n- (b) *The margin trap*: traffic recovers but only through discounting; early warning = SSS positive but gross margin per store down for 4 quarters.\n- (c) *The peso shock*: Fed hike + EM selloff; early warning = USD/MXN >19.5 and 10Y Mbono >10.5%.\n\n**Step 7-5. Decision Journal:** T0 = $121.13 (2026-08-24); Base IV = $122; Expected IV = $124; Key assumptions: margin 8.1%\u21929.2%, WACC 10.7%, g 4.5%. Red-team concerns: market already prices 9.5% margin; KOF excise tax; Valora integration.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 9. RED TEAM & ADVERSARIAL ANALYSIS (v2.0)\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n**Short thesis (bullets):**\n1. FEMSA's consolidated op margin (8.34% FY25) is structurally capped at ~8\u20139% by Valora (low margin) and pharmacy \u2014 it is no longer a \"quality compounder\" story; the equity is a retail conglomerate at a quality multiple.\n2. Q2-26 SSS \"close to double digits\" was ~60% World Cup; H2-26 will be subdued. The first negative-traffic flip was 2% \u2014 insufficient evidence of a durable turn.\n3. Tiendas 3B is growing >20%/yr and attacks OXXO's price-sensitive core; FEMSA's \"customer centricity\" reset is a defensive price war in disguise.\n4. Mexico beverage excise taxes are structural; KOF Mexico volumes were already soft in Q2-26 [Estimate].\n5. At $121, reverse-DCF requires a 2035 margin of ~9.5% \u2014 near the top of the achievable range, with no margin of safety.\n6. Consensus forward EPS growth is \u221213.4% [pack]; the next 12 months' earnings are falling, not rising.\n7. Governance: control-group structure with 0.0% reported insider ownership; the Levi & Korsinsky investigation is unresolved [Unconfirmed].\n\n**Logic combat (Long vs Short):**\n- Long logic strength: 6/10 (quality and dominance are real; but the valuation has no cushion)\n- Short logic strength: 5/10 (the margin-cap argument is credible but understates OXXO's pricing power and KOF's efficiency)\n- Gap < 2 \u2192 conviction capped at Medium. No buy rating possible at T0.\n\n**Killed arguments (and the conditions that would revive them):**\n- \"FEMSA is a cheap consumer staple at 16x forward earnings\" \u2014 killed by the negative-MoS; re-validates only if IV > $135, i.e., WACC <10.2% AND margin >9.5%.\n- \"The dividend is safe at 5%\" \u2014 mostly valid, but the extraordinary portion could be cut if FCF disappoints; monitor payout ratio.\n- \"KOF stake gives hidden asset value\" \u2014 partially valid; the SOTP already credits it.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 10. AUDIT RESULTS (v2.0 \u2014 domains A\u2013G, representative checks)\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u25